/** @page api_installed Installed C++ interfaces

The five project headers under `include/gige_mel/` are installed by
`GigeMelProvider`. Start with @ref md_docs_2consumer-integration "Integrating a MEL Consumer"
for installation and capture, then see @ref md_docs_2architecture "architecture"
and the @ref md_docs_2implementation-profile "MEL implementation profile".

Ordinary native MEL consumers use the pinned upstream factory declarations and
channels; this reference does not regenerate the upstream MEL API. The installed
project C++ backend contract is a **source-level integration contract, not a
stable cross-toolchain plugin ABI**. The upstream factory lookup symbols have C
linkage but use C++ types and are not a C API.

Header | Entry points
------ | ------------
@ref include/gige_mel/provider.hpp "provider.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::make_api_manager, @ref gige_mel::ProviderSettings, @ref gige_mel::ProviderStatistics and @ref gige_mel::provider_statistics
@ref include/gige_mel/backend.hpp "backend.hpp" | @ref installed_backend_contracts
@ref include/gige_mel/navigation.hpp "navigation.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::NavigationReport
@ref include/gige_mel/line_of_sight.hpp "line_of_sight.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::LosSupport and @ref gige_mel::backend::LosObservation
@ref include/gige_mel/image_field_of_view.hpp "image_field_of_view.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::ImageFieldOfView and @ref gige_mel::backend::IImageFieldOfViewSource
@ref include/gige_mel/task_execution.hpp "task_execution.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::ITaskExecutionSource and @ref gige_mel::backend::ITaskExecutionSession

@section installed_backend_contracts Backend Contracts

- Select a backend with @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraBackend and open an
  @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraDevice. See @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraBackend::open "open()"
  for identity and @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraDevice::apply "apply()" for effective readback.
- Read @ref gige_mel::backend::ErrorCode and @ref gige_mel::backend::Result for error
  handling, then @ref gige_mel::backend::CameraConfiguration,
  @ref gige_mel::backend::CameraCapabilities and @ref gige_mel::backend::image_layout
  for geometry, timing and storage.
- For adapter examples and acceptance tests, see
  @ref md_docs_2backend-authoring "Adding a camera backend".

@subsection installed_frame_ownership Frame and Stream Ownership

Discover sources with @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraDevice::stream_topology
and select transports in @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraDevice::start_acquisition.
The returned @ref gige_mel::backend::IFrameStream receivers are already started.
Follow each receiver through
@ref gige_mel::backend::IFrameStream::receive "receive()" and
@ref gige_mel::backend::IFrameStream::request_stop "request_stop()". See
@ref gige_mel::backend::FrameDescriptor and @ref gige_mel::backend::FrameTimestamp
for admission and timing, and @ref gige_mel::backend::FrameLease for native
ownership versus explicit MEL buffer release.

@subsection installed_optional_capabilities Optional Navigation, FOV, LOS, Stack and Task Interfaces

- Virtual tasking: @ref gige_mel::backend::ITaskExecutionSource opens an owned
  @ref gige_mel::backend::ITaskExecutionSession. The
  @ref md_docs_2task-scheduling-provider "virtual stare profile" specifies
  admission, replacement, cancellation and retirement. Only a recording fixture
  qualifies it; it does not grant physical control authority.
- Navigation input: @ref gige_mel::backend::INavigationSink and
  @ref gige_mel::backend::INavigationSink::submit_navigation "submit_navigation()".
- Image optics: @ref gige_mel::backend::IImageFieldOfViewSource::image_field_of_view "image_field_of_view()"
  resolves two angles for the frozen actual configuration before acquisition.
  Only absence selects the session-pitch model; explicit errors fail enable.
  This source-level C++ extension is fixture-qualified only and does not apply to Stack.
- LOS output: @ref gige_mel::backend::ILineOfSightSource,
  @ref gige_mel::backend::ILineOfSightSource::open_line_of_sight "open_line_of_sight()"
  and @ref gige_mel::backend::ILineOfSightStream.
- Stack output: @ref gige_mel::backend::IStackedImageSource,
  @ref gige_mel::backend::IStackedImageSource::open_stacked_images "open_stacked_images()",
  @ref gige_mel::backend::IStackedImageStream, @ref gige_mel::backend::StackSupport
  and @ref gige_mel::backend::StackLease.

The presence of a C++ interface is not a guarantee that a source supports the
capability; see @ref md_docs_2status "current capability and evidence status".

@section installed_contract_evidence Contract evidence and limits

- `backend_contract` and `provider_backend_portability` cover exact open,
  configuration readback, padded rows, source lease retention and stop/close.
- `provider_contract` covers registered destination ownership, callback reentry,
  transient versus terminal receive results, timestamp rejection/discontinuity,
  partial configuration changes, and navigation receipt and submission errors.
- `provider_los_metadata`, `provider_stacked_image` and `provider_stack_admission`
  exercise capability gating, malformed input, cancellation and callback drain.
  The @ref md_docs_2qualification-evidence "qualification evidence" separates
  SDK-free fixtures from physical observations and open qualification gates.

The architecture overview's bootstrap limit of 16 Image buffers describes the
default, not a fixed maximum: @ref gige_mel::ProviderSettings controls the
per-channel limit. The Image descriptor checks do not prove an opaque owner's
pointer provenance or inspect Mono12 samples for high-nibble validity. Adapters
are responsible for both. These limits are not changes to provider behavior.
*/